  "worked_solution": "Newton\u2019s second law states that\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\nwhere $F$ is the *resultant* force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{4}-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t)+t)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e88{t}^{3}-2t,\\,\\frac{1}{t}+1\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resultant force $F$ at time $t$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =6\\cdot \u27e88{t}^{3}-2t,\\,\\frac{1}{t}+1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e848{t}^{3}-12t,\\,\\frac{6}{t}+6\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $t=1\\,\\text{s},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =\u27e848(1)^{3}-12(1),\\,\\frac{6}{1}+6\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e836,\\,12\u27e9\\,\\text{N}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
